# V.32bis at 12000 bit/s, 8 Sep 2026, with the rate chosen rather than
# pinned: this end offered everything it had and the two modems settled
# on 12000 through the R1/R2/R3 exchange.
#
# 12000 was held out of the offer for as long as it had only ever run
# down a pair of pipes at 30 dB.  This is the evidence that took it out
# of that category -- a real line, MNP class 4 negotiated over it, and a
# decision error that sat between 0.003 and 0.007 for the length of the
# call.  It is also the only fixture here whose rate is the product of a
# negotiation, so restrictRates, bestCommonRate and the rate signals all
# have to agree for it to come out at 12000 rather than 9600.
source:    recordings/20260907T234436-+15642442600.wav
seconds:   32.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis,v32,v22bis
v8:        yes
mnp:       4
connect:   V32bis 12000
expect:    https://2600.network - Patton 3120 #1
expect:    uSerNaME:
tolerance: 0
